WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.060
Hollywood loves remakes and reboots.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:08.600
Returning to time-tested franchises is irresistible
to big studios that know nostalgia is a hell

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.320
of a drug, and that there's plenty of new
money to be made when reviving an old cash

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.320
cow.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.400
There are so many remakes in the works, in
fact, that some might have slipped past your

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.400
radar.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.690
Here are a few awesome remakes you probably
didn't know were happening.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.560
Child's Play

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.080
Remakes are nothing new in the horror genre.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.550
And now it looks like a certain Good Guy doll
will terrorize a new generation of moviegoers.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.320
According to the Hollywood Reporter, MGM is
"fast-tracking" a Child's Play remake with

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.690
Norwegian director Lars Klevberg, produced
by the same guys who produced the 2017 It

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.690
remake.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.170
There's no word yet on who will star, but
as for the plot, Collider reports that the

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.140
new Child's Play will take a page from the
Stranger Things playbook, as it will involve

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.489
a group of kids working together to fight
the demonic doll.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:54.200
But things might get a bit messy in the Child's
Play universe.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.830
Universal Studios still intends to produce
a Chucky TV series and more sequels as part

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.129
of the original Child's Play franchise, all
starring Brad Dourif, the guy who's voiced

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.379
the wisecracking killer since 1988.

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:09.350
"No more Mr. Good Guy!"

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.970
The Witches

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.890
According to Variety, Forrest Gump and Back
to the Future director Robert Zemeckis is

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:20.500
remaking 1990's The Witches, a freaky film
based one of Roald Dahl's creepiest novels.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.380
The plot involves a young boy on vacation
who discovers a coven of witches that plans

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.049
on turning England's children into mice.

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:31.310
The original starred Anjelica Huston as the
villainous Grand High Witch, with a wonderfully

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.050
over-the-top German accent.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:37.470
The new version doesn't have a cast or a director
as of the making of this video, but it will

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.020
reportedly be more faithful to Dahl's novel.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.790
Guillermo del Toro was supposed to cast his
own spell on the remake, but now he's only

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.340
co-producing, alongside Gravity director Alfonso
Cuaron.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.350
With four Oscars and dozens of other awards
between the two of them, that's a lot of talent

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.900
behind the scenes, which gives us high hopes
for this remake.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.520
The Sword in the Stone

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.221
Continuing their streak of producing live-action
remakes of their classic animated films, Disney

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:05.990
is reportedly working on a new version of
1963's The Sword in the Stone.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:09.899
This whimsical cartoon told the familiar story
of a young King Arthur training under the

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:13.540
magical and musical tutelage of the wise old
wizard Merlin.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.639
"Hail King Arthur!

00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:17.739
Hail King Arthur!"

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:22.510
The first film was a lighthearted romp that
involved enchanted dishes, squirrel romance,

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.439
and a shapeshifting wizard battle.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:26.939
The remake, however, might be a tad darker.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:31.879
It's being directed by Juan Carlos Fresnadillo,
the guy behind 28 Weeks Later, and the screenplay

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.549
will be written by Bryan Cogman, who's written
multiple episodes of Game of Thrones.

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:40.499
So when the movie makes its premiere on Disney's
upcoming streaming service, expect something

00:02:40.499 --> 00:02:43.129
a bit more grown-up than the original.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.939
Uptown Saturday Night

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:49.999
Released in 1974, the original Uptown Saturday
Night features a big-name cast, including

00:02:49.999 --> 00:02:54.449
Sidney Poitier, Richard Pryor, Harry Belafonte
and Bill Cosby.

00:02:54.449 --> 00:02:58.030
The plot involves two buddies who get held
up after visiting a nightclub, and during

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.730
the robbery, they lose a lottery ticket worth
$50,000.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.139
Determined to get the ticket back, the duo
start searching for the crooks who made off

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:06.200
with their fortune.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.420
Anchorman director Adam McKay was initially
supposed to direct the upcoming remake, according

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.809
to the Hollywood Reporter, and the lead roles
were meant for Will Smith and Denzel Washington.

00:03:14.809 --> 00:03:18.809
Sadly, that never panned out, but now Kevin
Hart is tackling the project.

00:03:18.809 --> 00:03:22.360
There's no word yet on who will star opposite
him, but we do know the screenplay will be

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.389
written by Kenya Barris, the creator of ABC's
Black-ish.

00:03:26.389 --> 00:03:28.089
Point Blank

00:03:28.089 --> 00:03:32.200
Frank Grillo and Anthony Mackie have played
bitter enemies in the Captain America franchise,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.810
trading put-downs and punches as Crossbones
and Falcon, respectively.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.920
Now the two are going to butt heads again
in a remake of Point Blank, a 2010 French

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.249
action flick which boasts an impressive 91
percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:03:44.249 --> 00:03:47.529
According to Collider, Mackie will play a
nurse whose pregnant wife gets kidnapped by

00:03:47.529 --> 00:03:51.199
the brother of a hospitalized murder suspect
who wants to make a trade.

00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:55.579
As you can probably guess, Grillo plays the
murder suspect, and based off his antagonistic

00:03:55.579 --> 00:03:59.319
chemistry with Mackie in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, we're pretty sure Point Blank will

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.969
be one intense thriller when it premieres
on Netflix.

